            "failure_scenario": "No gate fails today (min_grade is B); the score drifts down with each PR that adds to mod.rs and the grade drops to A- or B within a few more.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "sibling_session_kv_add_add_conflict",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Five unmerged sibling branches (origin/devont/k1-serve-kv, devont/k1-kv-only, pr/4630, pr/4631, verify/6a-4606) carry crates/aprender-serve/src/gguf/cuda/session_kv.rs as blob cd1bced264, a different file from this PR head blob e2659c70ab. The sibling blob also defines session_kv_len and adds serving_kv_len / SERVE_BATCH_SLOTS / SERVE_FLOOR (serve-side sizing, #4630). Whichever lands second hits an add/add conflict on the same path and the same function name."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "command": [
              "git",
              "ls-tree",
              "refs/remotes/origin/<branch>",
              "--",
              "crates/aprender-serve/src/gguf/cuda/session_kv.rs"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "d0e0d23bb18c21eac750f5874a9c01cf800fcb3806821c9fc2eb45b529dbacd5",
            "failure_scenario": "#4630 and #4623 both merge to main; the second PR is DIRTY with an add/add conflict in session_kv.rs and its author hand-merges two different session_kv_len bodies, risking the serve-side floor and the chat-session floor of 2048 being silently unified.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "memory_probe_failure_reads_as_zero_free",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "mod.rs:798 `executor.memory_info().unwrap_or((0, 0))` turns a failed cudaMemGetInfo into 0 bytes free. Line 807 then sizes KV to the 2048 floor, and line 819 passes free=0 to serial_when_fp16_prefill_does_not_fit, so every QK-norm model satisfies need > free and is silently forced onto Serial prefill, the path whose 26k-token prefill timed out per the PR doc comment. The stderr line would read 0.0 GB is free."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "The unwrap_or line and its two uses were read at HEAD (git grep, rc 0, below); the failure mode needs memory_info() to return Err on a live device, which was not provoked (no GPU on this lane).",
            "command": [
              "git",
              "grep",
              "-n",
              "memory_info().unwrap_or((0, 0))",
              "HEAD",
              "--",
              "crates/aprender-serve/src/gguf/cuda/mod.rs"
            ],
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "767eb5efc79b46d6975e8c346a4a1839952dd062ac58937d5f23b4189dbfc659",
            "failure_scenario": "cudaMemGetInfo returns an error (context lost or driver reset) on a QK-norm model; build() proceeds with free=0, picks the 2048-position floor, prints 0.0 GB is free and forces Serial prefill, so the chat session is slow and short for a reason the log misattributes to VRAM. Guard: skip the fit check and the floor-clamp when memory_info() is Err.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "kv_not_recomputed_after_serial_fallback",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "After the fit check flips prefill to Serial (mod.rs:~814-826), max_seq_len is not recomputed. resident_estimate subtracted 3.5 GB of GH-178 workspace plus PREFILL_SCORES_BUDGET_BYTES (1 GiB, forward_qwen35_cuda_prefill.rs:49); only the 1 GiB score budget is recoverable on the serial path, about 7,000 positions at an 8B KV size, not the 4.6 GB the antigravity lane claims."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Agrees with the antigravity direction, disagrees with its magnitude. Read from source (git grep of the constant, rc 0); the position count is arithmetic from the PR doc comment KV size, not a run.",
            "failure_scenario": "A QK-norm model that fits only with a 1 GiB smaller reserve gets a KV capacity that many positions short after fallback; a long chat turn hits the context limit earlier than it needed to.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "fp16_message_printed_on_forced_serial",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "The [#3413] FP16 batched prefill message prints even when the path is Serial because BATCHED_PREFILL=0 was set explicitly."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "rationale": "Read from the diff only; the message ordering relative to the fit check was not run.",
            "failure_scenario": "An operator sets BATCHED_PREFILL=0, reads the FP16 batched prefill line in the log and concludes batched prefill is active; they chase a Serial-path slowdown in the wrong place.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
