          "ruleId": "cuda_malloc_unused_memory_supports_fit_check",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "NVIDIA docs say cudaMalloc allocates from unused device memory and list the allocation limit as available device memory; the PR sizing weights + cache + reserve + KV against free VRAM is consistent with that. No finding is raised; the query is recorded so asked-and-confirmed is distinguishable from not-asked."
          },
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "cited",
            "source": "nvidia-cuda-docs MCP (search_cuda_docs), cudaMalloc allocation limit = available device memory",
            "excerpt": "When invoked from the host, `cudaMalloc()` allocates a new region from unused device memory.",
            "excerpt_sha256": "db4535d33c03d0fdddf16b29704abc9b8ba150caba3f6a16b321bec599a25c55",
            "failure_scenario": "If free VRAM were not the bound on allocation, the fit check would admit a configuration that then fails at cudaMalloc; the docs excerpt says it is the bound.",
            "precision_class": "advisory"
          }
        }
      ]
